description:
FILED s543k (Opus 5.5, 2026-11-22), found by member 2's probe b05 (#5270): the span route (a file lexical used in a later package section) and the capture route (a file lexical a named sub captures) answer the same.  PRE-EXISTING: base 4a0fd0ec.

REPRODUCER (perl 5.40.3 | ./runpcl):
    sub early { defined(eval q{$x}) ? "d" : "u" }
    my $x = "lex";
    sub g { $x }
    print early(), " ", g(), "\n";
        perl  u lex        PCL  d lex

WHAT IT IS: the lexical is promoted under its OWN name (the identity cell: one declaration file-wide, the file never spells `$main::x`), so the cell IS the package variable `$main::x`; the eval in `early` gets no pair (the binder says its pad does not see the declaration -- right) and falls through to the package global, which is the lexical's cell.  s543k's #5270 fixed the MANGLED span cell (no M-F alias in the program unit); the identity cell has no alias to drop -- the shared symbol is the identity.  FIX DIRECTION (not designed): in a file with a string eval whose word does NOT see the declaration and that names the canon (Parser2::_eval_operand_may_name), take the mangle instead of identity (`_own_name_cell_ok` false); measure what moves (every identity cell in an eval file would become a mangle).
=== MEASURED, NOT FIXED (s543m, Opus 5.5, 2026-11-24) -- the brief's cure is far wider than the disease: STOPPED at the measurement, FLAGGED ===
THE MEASUREMENT (scratch/s543m/legs/m3-idmeas2.log, scratch/s543m/p3/idlog-wide.tsv in the s543m worktree): an instrumented snapshot of the s543m tree (an uncommitted _s543m_idmeas at the three identity-cell decisions: span, cspan, cap) transpiled the whole wide list (2,047 files: perl-tests, perl's t/, core lib, cpan-tests, everyday; `pl2cl < FILE`, so a .pm is read as a PROGRAM here).  For every identity decision it counted the string-eval WORDS (Parser2's _eval_words) whose pad does NOT see the binding (Binder::resolve at the word) and whose operand may name the canon (_eval_operand_may_name, the one reading).
  identity decisions: 1,432 in 466 files (212 of them not .pm);
  the brief's cure ("take the mangle when such a word exists") would MOVE 105 cells in 40 files -- 16 test programs (perl's t/base/lex.t, op/attrs.t, op/caller.t, op/method.t, op/sort.t, op/sprintf2.t, op/sub_lval.t, op/svleak.t, op/taint.t, op/write.t, uni/attrs.t, uni/fold.t; perl-tests caller.t, method.t, sort.t, sprintf2.t) and 24 modules read as programs (HTTP::Tiny 13 cells, Unicode::UCD 8, diagnostics 6, Test::More, Carp, Data::Dumper, Benchmark, Safe, Math::Complex, Module::Metadata, ExtUtils::*, ...);
  EVERY one of the 105 moves through a DYNAMIC operand (`eval $code` somewhere the declaration is not visible); through a LITERAL operand that spells the name: 0.
So the dynamic half of the rule is the whole cost, and the brief's stop condition ("more than a handful of real files move") holds.

THE SHAPES (scratch/s543m/p3/m3.pl, perl 5.40.3 | tree): `sub early { defined(eval q{$x}) ... } my $x = "lex"; sub g { $x }` u | d (the task's); a dynamic `eval '$' . $n` in a sub above: u | d; a sub defined in a BEGIN block above: u | d; `${"main::x"}` in a sub above -- NO eval at all: u | d (the identity cell IS $main::x: this face is #2642's, and no eval-word rule reaches it); an eval in a sub BELOW the declaration and at the top level after it: lex | lex (right); a qualified `$main::y2` spelled in the file: pkg lexy (right -- #470's mangle).

WHAT NOT TO RETRY: the eval-word rule with dynamic operands (40 files, every Moo / Sub::Quote / Test::More-style generated-code module that keeps a file lexical beside an `eval $code`).
THE NARROW OPTION (not built, for a ruling): mangle only where a LITERAL eval text that does not see the declaration spells the name -- 0 cells of the population move, the task's reproducer is fixed, the dynamic and the symbolic faces stay (they are #2642: the program's identity cell is the package variable of its name; s504c measured 77 identity promotions in perl-tests alone for the full cure).

FINAL SHAS (s543m, 2026-11-27, after the stacked rebase onto s543n 9a3ce86f and main 0be2848a; the notes above cite pre-rebase shas): no code (measured, not fixed).
